# Canonical identity for the git history. 30 of the early commits were made with a placeholder
# author (`n <x@y.z>`) and most of the rest with a machine-local hostname address. A Zenodo or
# GitHub archive inherits whatever the log says, so the mapping is fixed here rather than by
# rewriting history, which would invalidate every commit hash referenced in the docs.
#
# The canonical NAME is the one on the paper, CITATION.cff, LICENSE and the ORCID record. The
# log used a shorter form, so an archive built from it credited the software to a name that
# matched no published artefact.
Nirmalkumar Thirupallikrishnan Kesavan <thirupallikrishnan.n@northeastern.edu>
Nirmalkumar Thirupallikrishnan Kesavan <thirupallikrishnan.n@northeastern.edu> <nirmalkumar@Nirmals-MacBook-Air.local>
Nirmalkumar Thirupallikrishnan Kesavan <thirupallikrishnan.n@northeastern.edu> <nk31dec2002@gmail.com>
Nirmalkumar Thirupallikrishnan Kesavan <thirupallikrishnan.n@northeastern.edu> <x@y.z>
